        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c87656c9-d468-59c8-a429-2bb749088889",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game\n- Places: BB&T Center, Sunrise, Florida, Winter Haven, Florida\n- Organizations: Florida Panthers, Florida House of Representatives\n- People: Baxter Troutman\n- Topics: 2002–03 NHL season, 2002–03 Florida Panthers season\n\nFacts:\n- The BB&T Center is an indoor arena in Sunrise, Florida, and it was previously known as the National Car Rental Center, Office Depot Center, and BankAtlantic Center.\n- The BB&T Center was completed in 1998 at a cost of US$185 million, was almost entirely publicly financed, and includes 70 suites and 2,623 club seats.\n- The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game took place on February 2, 2003, during the 2002–03 NHL season at the Office Depot Center in Sunrise, Florida.\n- The Office Depot Center was the home arena of the Florida Panthers when it hosted the 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game.\n- During the 2002–03 Florida Panthers season, the Florida Panthers did not make the playoffs but did host the 53rd All-Star Game.\n- Baxter Troutman is a citrus grower, businessman, and Republican politician from Winter Haven, Florida.\n- Baxter Troutman served as the representative for District 66 in the Florida House of Representatives.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
